window.LEARN_CONTENT=window.LEARN_CONTENT||{};window.LEARN_CONTENT["a-2908d6b44ee04c2d"]={"zh":"<p><a id=\"export-and-track-security-findings\"></a></p> <h1 id=\"_1\">导出和跟踪安全发现项</h1> <blockquote> <p>完整文档索引请参阅 <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt（需联网）</a>。如需查看文档的 Markdown 版本，可在页面 URL 末尾追加 <code>.md</code>。</p> </blockquote> <p>使用已完成的 Codex Security 扫描，可以执行以下任一交接操作：</p> <ul> <li><strong>导出：</strong> 创建可携带的 JSON、CSV 或 SARIF 文件。</li> <li><strong>跟踪发现项：</strong> 将选定的发现项整理成 Linear、GitHub 或 Jira 问题，或创建一份私密的 GitHub Security Advisory 草稿。Codex 会检查重复项，并在获得你的批准前等待，不会写入外部系统。</li> </ul> <p>这两种工作流程都不会更改已封存的扫描包。</p> <p>可用的产物链接和导出格式取决于你使用的 Codex 界面及已安装的插件版本。将格式用于自动化之前，请查看<a href=\"#/article/a-796d8353993fb17e\">插件变更记录</a>。</p> <p><a id=\"export-a-portable-artifact\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_2\">导出可携带的产物</h2> <p>在桌面应用中，打开 <strong>Security</strong> &gt; <strong>Scans</strong> 下的一次已完成扫描。使用可用的产物链接检查 <code>report.md</code>、<code>findings.json</code>、<code>scan-manifest.json</code>、<code>coverage.json</code>，或存在时的 SARIF 报告。</p> <p>若要创建其他受支持的格式，请要求 Codex 从已完成的扫描中导出发现项，同时不要更改已封存的扫描包：</p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Export the findings from [completed scan directory] as [JSON, CSV, or SARIF]. Do not modify the sealed scan bundle or upload its contents.\n</code></pre><div class=\"prompt-translation\"><div class=\"prompt-reference-heading\"><strong>提示词中文参考</strong><button class=\"copy-code copy-prompt-translation\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"复制中文参考\">复制中文</button></div><div class=\"prompt-reference-text\">将 [completed scan directory] 中的发现项导出为 [JSON, CSV, or SARIF]。不要修改已封存的扫描包，也不要上传其内容。</div></div> <p>根据目标位置选择合适的格式：</p> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>格式</th> <th>用途</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td>JSON</td> <td>为工具和脚本保留结构化、已封存的发现项。</td> </tr> <tr> <td>CSV</td> <td>在电子表格中检查发现项及当前本地分流状态。</td> </tr> <tr> <td>SARIF</td> <td>将发现项发送到支持 SARIF 交换格式的工具。</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <blockquote> <p>截图未离线保存: 已完成的 Codex Security 扫描，显示实际覆盖范围、发现项、清单、Markdown 报告和 SARIF 产物</p> </blockquote> <figcaption> 从已完成的扫描中打开覆盖信息、发现项、扫描清单、Markdown 报告或 SARIF 产物。 </figcaption> <p>选择 <strong>Markdown report</strong>，即可在系统配置的外部编辑器中打开 <code>report.md</code>。具体使用哪个编辑器取决于系统设置；下面展示生成的报告内容。</p> <blockquote> <p>截图未离线保存: 生成的安全报告示例，显示扫描范围、威胁模型和已验证的发现项</p> </blockquote> <figcaption> 在生成的 Markdown 报告中检查扫描范围、威胁模型、已验证的发现项和详细报告链接。 </figcaption> <p>使用返回的产物路径。如果其他工具需要完整的扫描上下文，请将原始 <code>scan-manifest.json</code>、<code>findings.json</code> 和 <code>coverage.json</code> 保存在一起。导出不会将发现项上传到代码扫描服务。</p> <p><a id=\"track-selected-findings\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_3\">跟踪选定的发现项</h2> <p>运行 <code>$codex-security:track-findings</code>，针对已验证的单个发现项，或同一次已封存扫描中的最多 25 个发现项进行处理。每次运行只使用一个提供方和一个目标位置。私密的 GitHub Security Advisory 草稿一次只能包含一个发现项。</p> <p>要准备 Linear 问题，请发送：</p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Use $codex-security:track-findings to prepare finding [finding ID] from\n[completed scan directory] for the Linear team [team] and project [project, if\nany]. Check for duplicates and show me the exact issue title, body, metadata,\nand destination. Do not create or update anything until I approve that payload.\n</code></pre><div class=\"prompt-translation\"><div class=\"prompt-reference-heading\"><strong>提示词中文参考</strong><button class=\"copy-code copy-prompt-translation\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"复制中文参考\">复制中文</button></div><div class=\"prompt-reference-text\">使用 $codex-security:track-findings，为 Linear 团队 [team] 和项目 [project, if\nany] 准备来自 [completed scan directory] 的发现项 [finding ID]。检查是否重复，\n向我展示确切的问题标题、正文、元数据\n和目标位置。在我批准这份待提交内容之前，不要创建或更新任何内容。</div></div> <p>要准备 GitHub 问题，请发送：</p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Use $codex-security:track-findings to prepare finding [finding ID] from\n[completed scan directory] for GitHub repository [owner/repository]. Check open\nand closed issues for duplicates and show me the exact issue title, body,\nmetadata, repository visibility, and authenticated transport. Do not create or\nupdate anything until I approve that payload.\n</code></pre><div class=\"prompt-translation\"><div class=\"prompt-reference-heading\"><strong>提示词中文参考</strong><button class=\"copy-code copy-prompt-translation\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"复制中文参考\">复制中文</button></div><div class=\"prompt-reference-text\">使用 $codex-security:track-findings，为 GitHub 仓库 [owner/repository] 准备来自\n[completed scan directory] 的发现项 [finding ID]。检查未关闭和\n已关闭的问题，确认是否重复，并向我展示确切的问题标题、正文、\n元数据、仓库可见性，以及经过身份验证的传输方式。在我批准这份待提交内容之前，不要创建或\n更新任何内容。</div></div> <p>要准备 Jira 问题，请发送：</p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Use $codex-security:track-findings to prepare finding [finding ID] from\n[completed scan directory] for Jira project [project key] as [issue type].\nCheck for duplicates and show me the exact issue summary, description,\nmetadata, and destination. Do not create or update anything until I approve\nthat payload.\n</code></pre><div class=\"prompt-translation\"><div class=\"prompt-reference-heading\"><strong>提示词中文参考</strong><button class=\"copy-code copy-prompt-translation\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"复制中文参考\">复制中文</button></div><div class=\"prompt-reference-text\">使用 $codex-security:track-findings，将来自 [completed scan directory] 的\n发现项 [finding ID] 准备为 Jira 项目 [project key] 中的 [issue type]。\n检查是否重复，并向我展示确切的问题摘要、描述、\n元数据和目标位置。在我批准这份待提交内容之前，不要创建或更新\n任何内容。</div></div> <p>在 Codex 中跟踪 Jira 问题需要 Atlassian Rovo 插件。复用现有问题需要读取权限；创建或更新问题需要读取和写入权限。</p> <p>要准备一份私密的 GitHub Security Advisory 草稿，请发送：</p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Use $codex-security:track-findings to prepare finding [finding ID] from\n[completed scan directory] as a private draft GitHub Security Advisory in\n[owner/repository]. Verify the sealed source revision, repository, affected\npaths, package metadata, and duplicate state. Show me the exact advisory\npayload, authenticated GitHub CLI identity, and disclosure warnings. Do not\ncreate anything until I approve that payload.\n</code></pre><div class=\"prompt-translation\"><div class=\"prompt-reference-heading\"><strong>提示词中文参考</strong><button class=\"copy-code copy-prompt-translation\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"复制中文参考\">复制中文</button></div><div class=\"prompt-reference-text\">使用 $codex-security:track-findings，将来自 [completed scan directory] 的\n发现项 [finding ID] 准备为 [owner/repository] 中私密的 GitHub Security Advisory 草稿。\n核实封存的源代码修订版本、仓库、受影响的\n路径、软件包元数据以及重复状态。向我展示确切的安全公告\n待提交内容、经过身份验证的 GitHub CLI 身份，以及披露警告。在我\n批准这份待提交内容之前，不要创建任何内容。</div></div> <p>草稿公告必须只包含一项发现，并且该发现必须来自 <code>git_revision</code> 扫描。还必须提供已验证的公开规范源代码仓库，并具有管理员访问权限。此流程不能批量处理公告，也不能更新、发布或关闭公告。如果源代码仓库不符合这些要求，请改用私密问题跟踪位置。</p> <p><a id=\"review-the-proposed-write\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_4\">审核拟议写入内容</h2> <ol> <li>确认发现项 ID 和指纹来自预期的已封存扫描。</li> <li>确认提供方、准确的 Linear 团队、GitHub 仓库、Jira 项目或公告仓库，以及目标位置当前的可见范围。</li> <li>检查重复项处理结果：<code>create</code>、<code>reuse</code>、<code>update</code> 或 <code>blocked</code>。</li> <li>阅读完整的拟议标题、正文、源代码位置和提供方元数据。删除目标位置不应公开的漏洞利用细节或内部证据。</li> <li>只批准这份确切内容。如果目标位置、可见范围、发现项集合或正文发生变化，必须重新预览。</li> </ol> <p>敏感发现项应发送到私密目标位置。在内部或公开 GitHub 仓库中创建问题时，系统必须明确警告其可见范围，并要求你批准完整内容。请将公告草稿描述视为将来可能公开的内容；批准前删除凭据、私密证据和不必要的漏洞利用细节。</p> <p>请在 Codex 对话中审核并批准外部操作。批准并不会在 Security 工作台中创建单独的问题或公告页面。</p> <p><a id=\"verify-the-tracked-item\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_5\">验证已跟踪的条目</h2> <p>你批准拟议写入后，Codex 会重新检查已封存的来源、目标位置、访问权限和重复项状态。批量处理时会逐项处理发现项，并在遇到第一个不确定结果时停止。只有 Codex 重新读取确切的问题，并验证其关联标识符和内容后，创建、更新或复用操作才算完成。</p> <p>请将返回的规范问题或公告 URL 与分流记录一起保存。负责人决定修复该条目后，请继续阅读<a href=\"#/article/a-44471eb3eae1b363\">修复并验证发现项</a>。</p>","en":"<h1 id=\"export-and-track-security-findings\">Export and track security findings</h1> <blockquote> <p>For the complete documentation index, see <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt (online)</a>. Markdown versions of documentation pages are available by appending <code>.md</code> to the page URL.</p> </blockquote> <p>Use a completed Codex Security scan for either of these handoffs:</p> <ul> <li><strong>Export</strong> creates a portable JSON, CSV, or SARIF file.</li> <li><strong>Track findings</strong> prepares selected findings as Linear, GitHub, or Jira issues, or as one private draft GitHub Security Advisory. Codex checks for duplicates and waits for your approval before writing.</li> </ul> <p>Neither workflow changes the sealed scan bundle.</p> <p>Available artifact links and export formats depend on your Codex surface and installed plugin version. Check the <a href=\"#/article/a-796d8353993fb17e\">plugin changelog</a> before you use a format in automation.</p> <h2 id=\"export-a-portable-artifact\">Export a portable artifact</h2> <p>In the desktop app, open a completed scan from <strong>Security</strong> &gt; <strong>Scans</strong>. Use its available artifact links to inspect <code>report.md</code>, <code>findings.json</code>, <code>scan-manifest.json</code>, <code>coverage.json</code>, or a SARIF report when present.</p> <p>To create another supported format, ask Codex to export findings from the completed scan without modifying its sealed bundle:</p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Export the findings from [completed scan directory] as [JSON, CSV, or SARIF]. Do not modify the sealed scan bundle or upload its contents.\n</code></pre> <p>Choose the format that fits your destination:</p> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>Format</th> <th>Use it for</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td>JSON</td> <td>Preserve the sealed structured findings for tools and scripts.</td> </tr> <tr> <td>CSV</td> <td>Review findings and current local triage state in a spreadsheet.</td> </tr> <tr> <td>SARIF</td> <td>Send findings to tools that support the SARIF interchange format.</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <blockquote> <p>Screenshot not stored offline: Completed Codex Security scan showing the real coverage, findings, manifest, Markdown, and SARIF artifacts</p> </blockquote> <figcaption> Open the coverage, findings, scan manifest, Markdown report, or SARIF artifact from a completed scan. </figcaption> <p>Select <strong>Markdown report</strong> to open <code>report.md</code> in your configured external editor. The editor depends on your system settings; the example below shows the generated report contents.</p> <blockquote> <p>Screenshot not stored offline: Example generated security report showing the scan scope, threat model, and validated findings</p> </blockquote> <figcaption> Review the scan scope, threat model, validated findings, and detailed report links in the generated Markdown report. </figcaption> <p>Use the returned artifact path. If another tool needs the complete scan context, keep the original <code>scan-manifest.json</code>, <code>findings.json</code>, and <code>coverage.json</code> together. Exporting doesn't upload findings to a code-scanning service.</p> <h2 id=\"track-selected-findings\">Track selected findings</h2> <p>Run <code>$codex-security:track-findings</code> with one validated finding or an selected batch of up to 25 findings from the same sealed scan. Each run uses one provider and one destination. A private draft GitHub Security Advisory accepts only one finding.</p> <p>To prepare a Linear issue, send:</p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Use $codex-security:track-findings to prepare finding [finding ID] from\n[completed scan directory] for the Linear team [team] and project [project, if\nany]. Check for duplicates and show me the exact issue title, body, metadata,\nand destination. Do not create or update anything until I approve that payload.\n</code></pre> <p>To prepare a GitHub issue, send:</p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Use $codex-security:track-findings to prepare finding [finding ID] from\n[completed scan directory] for GitHub repository [owner/repository]. Check open\nand closed issues for duplicates and show me the exact issue title, body,\nmetadata, repository visibility, and authenticated transport. Do not create or\nupdate anything until I approve that payload.\n</code></pre> <p>To prepare a Jira issue, send:</p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Use $codex-security:track-findings to prepare finding [finding ID] from\n[completed scan directory] for Jira project [project key] as [issue type].\nCheck for duplicates and show me the exact issue summary, description,\nmetadata, and destination. Do not create or update anything until I approve\nthat payload.\n</code></pre> <p>Jira tracking requires the Atlassian Rovo plugin in Codex. Reusing an issue requires read access; creating or updating one requires read and write access.</p> <p>To prepare a private draft GitHub Security Advisory, send:</p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Use $codex-security:track-findings to prepare finding [finding ID] from\n[completed scan directory] as a private draft GitHub Security Advisory in\n[owner/repository]. Verify the sealed source revision, repository, affected\npaths, package metadata, and duplicate state. Show me the exact advisory\npayload, authenticated GitHub CLI identity, and disclosure warnings. Do not\ncreate anything until I approve that payload.\n</code></pre> <p>Draft advisories require one finding from a sealed <code>git_revision</code> scan, the verified public canonical source repository, and administrator access. The workflow doesn't batch, update, publish, or close advisories. Use a private issue destination when the source doesn't meet those requirements.</p> <h2 id=\"review-the-proposed-write\">Review the proposed write</h2> <ol> <li>Confirm the finding ID and fingerprint came from the intended sealed scan.</li> <li>Confirm the provider, exact Linear team, GitHub repository, Jira project, or advisory repository, and the live destination visibility.</li> <li>Review the duplicate outcome: <code>create</code>, <code>reuse</code>, <code>update</code>, or <code>blocked</code>.</li> <li>Read the complete proposed title, body, source locations, and provider metadata. Remove exploit detail or internal evidence that the destination shouldn't expose.</li> <li>Approve only that exact payload. A changed destination, visibility, finding set, or body requires a new preview.</li> </ol> <p>Sensitive findings should go to a private destination. Creating an issue in an internal or public GitHub repository requires an explicit visibility warning and approval of the complete content. Treat a draft advisory description as eventually public and remove credentials, private evidence, and unnecessary exploit details before approval.</p> <p>Review and approve external actions in the Codex conversation. Approval doesn't create a separate issue or advisory screen in the Security workbench.</p> <h2 id=\"verify-the-tracked-item\">Verify the tracked item</h2> <p>After you approve the proposed write, Codex rechecks the sealed source, destination, access, and duplicate state. For a batch, it processes findings one at a time and stops at the first uncertain result. Creation, update, or reuse is complete only after Codex reads the exact issue back and verifies its binding identifiers and content.</p> <p>Keep the returned canonical issue or advisory URL with your triage record. Continue with <a href=\"#/article/a-44471eb3eae1b363\">Fix and verify a finding</a> when the owner accepts the item for remediation.</p>"};
